<title>GERMANY: Lufthansa walkout hits 92 flights.</title>
<headline>Lufthansa walkout hits 92 flights.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>German airline Lufthansa AG said on Thursday that a total of 92 German and European flights and 6,500 passengers were affected by a two-hour walkout early on Thursday, a spokesman said.</p>
<p>Lufthansa spokesman Georg-Hermann Fahler told Reuters that 18 flights in Frankfurt were also affected by the work stoppage of flight staff and technical workers in the DAG white-collar workers union.</p>
<p>He said three special flights were staffed by management crew, with Boeing 747s sent from Frankfurt to Hamburg and Munich and an Airbus A340 sent to Munich.</p>
<p>DAG represents mainly flight personnel and white-collar workers at Lufthansa while the OeTV union represents mainly blue collar and ground personnel.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
